---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
---
<Gallery title="Pattern: inline validation summary">
  <p class="demo-note">
    On submit, if the form is invalid: list every problem field up top, move focus to
    that summary first (not straight into a field — a screen-reader user hears the
    overview before jumping in), and let each link focus its exact field. Composed
    entirely from existing components — the summary box is just <code>.bo-alert
    bo-alert--danger</code>, and every field's error state (red border, red label,
    required asterisk) comes free from the existing <code>:user-invalid</code> styling
    already in <code>.bo-form-field</code>. Try it: submit the empty form below.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <form data-validation-summary novalidate hx-boost="false">
      <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
        <p><strong>There is a problem</strong></p>
        <ul></ul>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="bo-form-section">
        <legend class="bo-form-section__legend">New purchase order</legend>
        <div class="bo-form-row">
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="vs-vendor">Vendor</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="vs-vendor" required />
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="vs-amount">Amount</label>
            <input class="bo-input bo-input--numeric" id="vs-amount" type="number" min="0" step="0.01" required />
          </div>
          <div class="bo-form-field">
            <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="vs-email">Approver email</label>
            <input class="bo-input" id="vs-email" type="email" required />
          </div>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="bo-form-actions">
        <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Submit</button>
      </div>
    </form>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initValidationSummary } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initValidationSummary();
  </script>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Markup</h2>
    <pre><code>{`<form data-validation-summary>
  <div class="bo-alert bo-alert--danger" data-validation-summary-box hidden role="alert">
    <p>There is a problem</p>
    <ul></ul>  <!-- populated on an invalid submit -->
  </div>
  <div class="bo-form-field">
    <label class="bo-form-field__label" for="vendor">Vendor</label>
    <input class="bo-input" id="vendor" required />
  </div>
  ...
</form>

<script type="module">
  import { initValidationSummary } from "@busy-office/ui/js";
  initValidationSummary(); // once — wires the [data-validation-summary] form
</script>`}</code></pre>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">Field labels come from each field's own <code>&lt;label
    for&gt;</code> text — no extra markup needed to name a field in the summary list.</p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><strong>If your app boosts forms with <code>htmx</code>'s
    <code>hx-boost</code></strong> (as this docs site does — found live while building
    this demo): add <code>hx-boost="false"</code> to any
    <code>[data-validation-summary]</code> form. Without it, htmx's own submit
    interception races this behavior's — htmx fetches and swaps the page before (or
    instead of) the summary rendering, so the failed-validation state never sticks.</p>
  </section>

  <Related links={[
    ["/components/alerts", "Alerts & toasts"],
    ["/components/form", "Forms"],
    ["/concepts/js-behaviors", "JS behaviors"],
    ["/patterns/login", "Login pattern"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
